---@alias gcp.testing_v1.TestExecutionStateEnum "TEST_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"VALIDATING"|"PENDING"|"RUNNING"|"FINISHED"|"ERROR"|"UNSUPPORTED_ENVIRONMENT"|"INCOMPATIBLE_ENVIRONMENT"|"INCOMPATIBLE_ARCHITECTURE"|"CANCELLED"|"INVALID"

---TestMatrix captures all details about a test. It contains the environment configuration, test specification, test executions and overall state and outcome.
---@class gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrix
---@field extendedInvalidMatrixDetails? gcp.testing_v1.MatrixErrorDetailList Output only. Details about why a matrix was deemed invalid. If multiple checks can be safely performed, they will be reported but no assumptions should be made about the length of this list.
---@field flakyTestAttempts? number The number of times a TestExecution should be re-attempted if one or more of its test cases fail for any reason. The maximum number of reruns allowed is 10. Default is 0, which implies no reruns.
---@field testExecutions? gcp.testing_v1.TestExecutionList Output only. The list of test executions that the service creates for this matrix.
---@field testSpecification? gcp.testing_v1.TestSpecification Required. How to run the test.
---@field invalidMatrixDetails? gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrixInvalidMatrixDetailsEnum Output only. Describes why the matrix is considered invalid. Only useful for matrices in the INVALID state.
---@field testMatrixId? string Output only. Unique id set by the service.
---@field resultStorage? gcp.testing_v1.ResultStorage Required. Where the results for the matrix are written.
---@field projectId? string The cloud project that owns the test matrix.
---@field clientInfo? gcp.testing_v1.ClientInfo Information about the client which invoked the test.
---@field outcomeSummary? gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrixOutcomeSummaryEnum Output Only. The overall outcome of the test. Only set when the test matrix state is FINISHED.
---@field timestamp? string Output only. The time this test matrix was initially created.
---@field state? gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrixStateEnum Output only. Indicates the current progress of the test matrix.
---@field environmentMatrix? gcp.testing_v1.EnvironmentMatrix Required. The devices the tests are being executed on.
---@field failFast? boolean If true, only a single attempt at most will be made to run each execution/shard in the matrix. Flaky test attempts are not affected. Normally, 2 or more attempts are made if a potential infrastructure issue is detected. This feature is for latency sensitive workloads. The incidence of execution failures may be significantly greater for fail-fast matrices and support is more limited because of that expectation.

---@alias gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrixInvalidMatrixDetailsEnum "INVALID_MATRIX_DETAILS_UNSPECIFIED"|"DETAILS_UNAVAILABLE"|"MALFORMED_APK"|"MALFORMED_TEST_APK"|"NO_MANIFEST"|"NO_PACKAGE_NAME"|"INVALID_PACKAGE_NAME"|"TEST_SAME_AS_APP"|"NO_INSTRUMENTATION"|"NO_SIGNATURE"|"INSTRUMENTATION_ORCHESTRATOR_INCOMPATIBLE"|"NO_TEST_RUNNER_CLASS"|"NO_LAUNCHER_ACTIVITY"|"FORBIDDEN_PERMISSIONS"|"INVALID_ROBO_DIRECTIVES"|"INVALID_RESOURCE_NAME"|"INVALID_DIRECTIVE_ACTION"|"TEST_LOOP_INTENT_FILTER_NOT_FOUND"|"SCENARIO_LABEL_NOT_DECLARED"|"SCENARIO_LABEL_MALFORMED"|"SCENARIO_NOT_DECLARED"|"DEVICE_ADMIN_RECEIVER"|"MALFORMED_XC_TEST_ZIP"|"BUILT_FOR_IOS_SIMULATOR"|"NO_TESTS_IN_XC_TEST_ZIP"|"USE_DESTINATION_ARTIFACTS"|"TEST_NOT_APP_HOSTED"|"PLIST_CANNOT_BE_PARSED"|"TEST_ONLY_APK"|"MALFORMED_IPA"|"MISSING_URL_SCHEME"|"MALFORMED_APP_BUNDLE"|"NO_CODE_APK"|"INVALID_INPUT_APK"|"INVALID_APK_PREVIEW_SDK"|"MATRIX_TOO_LARGE"|"TEST_QUOTA_EXCEEDED"|"SERVICE_NOT_ACTIVATED"|"UNKNOWN_PERMISSION_ERROR"

---@alias gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrixOutcomeSummaryEnum "OUTCOME_SUMMARY_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUCCESS"|"FAILURE"|"INCONCLUSIVE"|"SKIPPED"

---@alias gcp.testing_v1.TestMatrixStateEnum "TEST_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"VALIDATING"|"PENDING"|"RUNNING"|"FINISHED"|"ERROR"|"UNSUPPORTED_ENVIRONMENT"|"INCOMPATIBLE_ENVIRONMENT"|"INCOMPATIBLE_ARCHITECTURE"|"CANCELLED"|"INVALID"

---A description of how to set up the Android device prior to running the test.
---@class gcp.testing_v1.TestSetup
---@field account? gcp.testing_v1.Account The device will be logged in on this account for the duration of the test.
---@field systrace? gcp.testing_v1.SystraceSetup Systrace configuration for the run. Deprecated: Systrace used Python 2 which was sunsetted on 2020-01-01. Systrace is no longer supported in the Cloud Testing API, and no Systrace file will be provided in the results.
---@field initialSetupApks? gcp.testing_v1.ApkList Optional. Initial setup APKs to install before the app under test is installed. Limited to a combined total of 100 initial setup and additional files.
---@field directoriesToPull? gcp.testing_v1.StringList List of directories on the device to upload to GCS at the end of the test; they must be absolute paths under /sdcard, /storage or /data/local/tmp. Path names are restricted to characters a-z A-Z 0-9 _ - . + and / Note: The paths /sdcard and /data will be made available and treated as implicit path substitutions. E.g. if /sdcard on a particular device does not map to external storage, the system will replace it with the external storage path prefix for that device.
---@field environmentVariables? gcp.testing_v1.EnvironmentVariableList Environment variables to set for the test (only applicable for instrumentation tests).
---@field networkProfile? string The network traffic profile used for running the test. Available network profiles can be queried by using the NETWORK_CONFIGURATION environment type when calling TestEnvironmentDiscoveryService.GetTestEnvironmentCatalog.
---@field additionalApks? gcp.testing_v1.ApkList APKs to install in addition to those being directly tested. These will be installed after the app under test. Limited to a combined total of 100 initial setup and additional files.
---@field filesToPush? gcp.testing_v1.DeviceFileList List of files to push to the device before starting the test.
---@field dontAutograntPermissions? boolean Whether to prevent all runtime permissions to be granted at app install

---A description of how to run the test.
---@class gcp.testing_v1.TestSpecification
---@field androidRoboTest? gcp.testing_v1.AndroidRoboTest An Android robo test.
---@field androidTestLoop? gcp.testing_v1.AndroidTestLoop An Android Application with a Test Loop.
---@field testTimeout? string Max time a test execution is allowed to run before it is automatically cancelled. The default value is 5 min.
---@field disableVideoRecording? boolean Disables video recording. May reduce test latency.
---@field testSetup? gcp.testing_v1.TestSetup Test setup requirements for Android e.g. files to install, bootstrap scripts.
---@field androidInstrumentationTest? gcp.testing_v1.AndroidInstrumentationTest An Android instrumentation test.
---@field iosRoboTest? gcp.testing_v1.IosRoboTest An iOS Robo test.
---@field iosTestLoop? gcp.testing_v1.IosTestLoop An iOS application with a test loop.
---@field iosTestSetup? gcp.testing_v1.IosTestSetup Test setup requirements for iOS.
---@field iosXcTest? gcp.testing_v1.IosXcTest An iOS XCTest, via an .xctestrun file.
---@field disablePerformanceMetrics? boolean Disables performance metrics recording. May reduce test latency.

---Test targets for a shard.
---@class gcp.testing_v1.TestTargetsForShard
---@field testTargets? gcp.testing_v1.StringList Group of packages, classes, and/or test methods to be run for each shard. The targets need to be specified in AndroidJUnitRunner argument format. For example, "package com.my.packages" "class com.my.package.MyClass". The number of test_targets must be greater than 0.

---@alias gcp.testing_v1.TestTargetsForShardList gcp.testing_v1.TestTargetsForShard[]

---Represents a whole or partial calendar date, such as a birthday. The time of day and time zone are either specified elsewhere or are insignificant. The date is relative to the Gregorian Calendar. This can represent one of the following: * A full date, with non-zero year, month, and day values. * A month and day, with a zero year (for example, an anniversary). * A year on its own, with a zero month and a zero day. * A year and month, with a zero day (for example, a credit card expiration date). Related types: * google.type.TimeOfDay * google.type.DateTime * google.protobuf.Timestamp
---@class gcp.testing_v1.Testing_Date
---@field month? number Month of a year. Must be from 1 to 12, or 0 to specify a year without a month and day.
---@field day? number Day of a month. Must be from 1 to 31 and valid for the year and month, or 0 to specify a year by itself or a year and month where the day isn't significant.
---@field year? number Year of the date. Must be from 1 to 9999, or 0 to specify a date without a year.

